{
  "case_id": "s12_one_broadcast_at_two_gateways_is_one_position",
  "title": "Copies of one position broadcast at two gateways are one position, timed by its first copy and precise when any copy qualifies",
  "rules": ["lnk_02", "pos_04"],
  "reasoning": [
    "warehouse-eng's reading for the link rules (PR #72, Decided without Casey): core keeps one row per delivery, so a broadcast heard by two gateways is two rows; lnk_02 reads them as one position, at the received_at of its first copy, as ADR 0005 times a delivery by its first sighting, and precise when any copy qualifies under pos_04.",
    "s12-ra's r20 broadcast (packet 12002) reached gateway s12-h1 on the public broker at 22 09:05:00 and s12-h2 on MeshSTL only at 09:05:02. It is one position, sent at 09:05:00, and it qualifies under pos_04 through the MeshSTL copy (20 bits). s12-ra is stationary on r20 at every receipt and on its hour box, so relayer_precise_source is true.",
    "s12-rb sent r20 on the public broker at 22 09:05 (packet 12004), and an r20 broadcast (packet 12005) whose public copy reached s12-h1 at 16 10:09:59 and whose MeshSTL copy reached s12-h2 at 16 10:10:01. That broadcast is timed 16 10:09:59, one second before the 7-day look-back of the first receipt (16 10:10:00), so no receipt reads it. s12-rb is stationary on r20 from packet 12004 alone, and relayer_precise_source is false. Read per delivery, the MeshSTL copy at 16 10:10:01 would be inside the first look-back and the flag would be true.",
    "Position copies uplinked by s12-h1 and s12-h2 are not radio deliveries at s12-g, so they make no candidate there; every receipt is a direct hop.",
    "Both hours: 2745.603337 m, kept with 3 packets, medians 6.0 dB and -95.0 dBm, position_uncertainty_m 386.484807 m, gateway not precise."
  ],
